* tb_threshold_accuracy: static trip point per select code of design/detector_top.spice
* (reference + REAL comparator + filter + flag logic), slow downward ramp of the monitored
* rail. Corner, temperature and detector supply are substituted by run.sh (default tt /
* 27 C / 3.3 V) so sim/ corner campaigns (#34) can drive this bench unchanged.
* The monitored rail is an IDEAL SOURCE here: row 5 is a static trip point, graded on a
* slow ramp (1 mV/us), not on a fast-edge stimulus. Trip = vmon when v(live) crosses 0.9 V
* (midpoint of the 1.44 V VOH / 0.36 V VOL output levels of the spec) on the way down.
* The ramp window is substituted by run.sh (RAMP_START / RAMP_END, default 1.9 -> 1.45 V)
* and always holds the 1 mV/us slew, so the stimulus RATE is identical whatever the window;
* only its extent moves. The window must SPAN the levels at the corner being run -- start
* above the highest trip point with the flag idle, end below the lowest -- or `meas` finds
* no crossing and the bench fails closed on the missing result (exit 3). Both ends are
* spec-derived, and both are needed because row 2's supply box moves every level:
*   start 1.9 V: clears the top of the LDO +/-2% window (1.836 V, row 8) by 64 mV and stays
*     inside row 1's 1.6-1.95 V rail range. The original 1.8 V start could not measure
*     code 00 at VSUP=3.63, where the level rises ABOVE 1.8 V: the live flag is already
*     asserted at t=0, there is no rising edge, and the bench exits 3 (that stuck-high
*     condition is the row 8 defect of #83, recorded in this bench's records/ as the
*     fail-closed transcript 2026-11-15-tb_threshold_accuracy-tt-vsup3p63-flag-stuck-high).
*   end 1.45 V: lowest level 1.584 V (row 4, 12% below nominal), minus row 5's +/-54 mV
*     fallback band, minus the ~73 mV the reference loses at row 2's 2.97 V corner = 1.457 V.
*     The original 1.55 V floor could not measure code 11 at VSUP=2.97 (level ~1.53 V).
* This bench grades a STATIC trip point on a slow sweep, so the window is free to span the
* levels; the droop-response benches (rows 6/7) are the ones that start from nominal.
* A corner campaign (#34) reaching past either end passes its own RAMP_START / RAMP_END
* rather than editing this deck.
.lib "__PDK_LIB__" __PROC__
.include "__NETLIST__"
.temp __TEMP__
.param vsup=__VSUP__
.option method=gear

Vrail rail 0 PWL(0 __RAMP_START__ 1n __RAMP_START__ __RAMP_US__u __RAMP_END__)
Vlo lo 0 0
Vhi hi 0 {vsup}
Vclr clr 0 0
Vd0 vd0 0 {vsup}
Vd1 vd1 0 {vsup}
Vd2 vd2 0 {vsup}
Vd3 vd3 0 {vsup}
X0 rail lo lo clr vd0 0 l0 st0 detector_top
X1 rail hi lo clr vd1 0 l1 st1 detector_top
X2 rail lo hi clr vd2 0 l2 st2 detector_top
X3 rail hi hi clr vd3 0 l3 st3 detector_top

.control
tran 50n __RAMP_US__u
meas tran vtrip_l0 find v(rail) when v(l0)=0.9 rise=1
echo "RESULT vtrip_l0 = $&vtrip_l0"
meas tran vtrip_l1 find v(rail) when v(l1)=0.9 rise=1
echo "RESULT vtrip_l1 = $&vtrip_l1"
meas tran vtrip_l2 find v(rail) when v(l2)=0.9 rise=1
echo "RESULT vtrip_l2 = $&vtrip_l2"
meas tran vtrip_l3 find v(rail) when v(l3)=0.9 rise=1
echo "RESULT vtrip_l3 = $&vtrip_l3"
meas tran idle_max_l0 max v(l0) from=2u to=20u
echo "RESULT idle_max_l0 = $&idle_max_l0"
meas tran idle_max_l1 max v(l1) from=2u to=20u
echo "RESULT idle_max_l1 = $&idle_max_l1"
meas tran idle_max_l2 max v(l2) from=2u to=20u
echo "RESULT idle_max_l2 = $&idle_max_l2"
meas tran idle_max_l3 max v(l3) from=2u to=20u
echo "RESULT idle_max_l3 = $&idle_max_l3"
quit
.endc
.end
